  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (ignoring probabilities) and then comparing the probabilities of exceeding this level. The aspiration level (1633.33) and the comparison of probabilities of positive deviations from it are central to the reason. However, the individual does not mention any such computation or reference point. Instead, the individual compares the two lotteries directly in terms of a trade-off between prize size and probability, focusing on the 100 Euro gain versus 1% loss. There is no indication that the individual calculated an average of all outcomes or assessed which outcomes exceed such a threshold. The justification is based on a marginal trade-off, not on deviations from an aspiration level. Therefore, the information considered and the decision rule used by the individual differ fundamentally from those required by the decision reason. The individual likely did not use the aspiration-level reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
